P00.4 Debian Trixie package compatibility probe
Date: 2026-10-28
Purpose: test whether Debian's stable WPE package provides a buildable backend for flutter_inappwebview_linux 0.1.0-beta.1.

Container: temporary Bookworm-derived container with Debian forky/sid packages; this is not a clean Debian Trixie image.
Selected packages:
  libwpewebkit-2.0-dev=2.48.3-1 (from Debian trixie)
  libwpewebkit-2.0-1=2.48.3-1 (from Debian trixie)
  libwpebackend-fdo-1.0-dev=1.16.1-1+b1 (from Debian forky/sid)
  flutter_inappwebview_linux=0.1.0-beta.1

Package inspection:
  pkg-config --modversion wpe-webkit-2.0 -> 2.48.3
  pkg-config --exists wpe-platform-2.0 -> not found
  libwpewebkit-2.0-dev contains no WPEPlatform headers
  the plugin CMake file selected its documented legacy FDO branch (HAVE_WPE_BACKEND_LEGACY=1)

Build attempts:
  First CMake generation stopped because the Trixie wpe-webkit-2.0.pc advertises a missing
  /usr/include/wpe-webkit-2.0/wpe-platform directory. To continue evaluating the legacy FDO
  branch only, an empty directory was created inside this temporary container; no repository or
  plugin source was changed.
  After flutter clean, flutter build linux --release exited 1 while compiling the plugin:
  in_app_webview.cc:6214:23: error: use of undeclared identifier 'webkit_web_view_get_theme_color'

Result: Debian Trixie's WPE 2.48.3 package plus the FDO backend does not build this plugin version.
No compatibility macro or plugin source patch was used. No application runtime replay was reached.
